    "description": "The caption under the grid preview on the General tab when gaps are on: the grid's size and the largest gap a placement keeps (it shrinks for a window too small to keep it). {cols} and {rows} are the grid's size, and the × between them stays. {gap} is the gap, a whole number, and {unit} is pt on macOS and px on Windows and stays as written. English says \"gaps\" even for 1, because the word counts the gaps between cells; a language whose plural needs a form for one may add it.",
    "placeholders": {
      "cols": {
        "type": "int",
        "example": "6"
      },
      "rows": {
        "type": "int",
        "example": "6"
      },
      "gap": {
        "type": "int",
        "example": "8"
      },
      "unit": {
        "type": "String",
        "example": "pt"
      }
    }
